1
00:00:02,355 --> 00:00:03,925
Popcorn's almost ready!

2
00:00:04,145 --> 00:00:05,745
Fresh out of the pan, careful, it's hot!

3
00:00:09,935 --> 00:00:11,705
Yakisoba is ready!

4
00:00:13,275 --> 00:00:14,205
- Ah!
- Good work!

5
00:00:14,205 --> 00:00:15,125
Thanks for your hard work!

6
00:00:15,149 --> 00:00:16,468
Hey, I'm here for a shift change!

7
00:00:17,275 --> 00:00:19,005
Huh? Where's Saeko?

8
00:00:19,435 --> 00:00:20,435
Hmm...

9
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:23,185
Haven't seen her today yet.

10
00:00:23,415 --> 00:00:24,544
Huh?

11
00:00:24,545 --> 00:00:27,055
Did she seriously oversleep
on day one of the festival?

12
00:00:27,435 --> 00:00:29,755
Why don't you give her a call?

13
00:00:30,575 --> 00:00:31,755
Oh, thanks.

14
00:00:31,885 --> 00:00:33,155
I'll call her in a bit.

15
00:00:34,155 --> 00:00:35,295
Let's go.

16
00:00:37,365 --> 00:00:38,695
Good work.

17
00:00:38,725 --> 00:00:39,964
Thanks, everyone!

18
00:00:39,965 --> 00:00:41,735
Miwa, have you seen Lucha?

19
00:00:42,785 --> 00:00:43,885
Haven't seen him.

20
00:00:44,375 --> 00:00:46,835
What the heck? Don't
tell me he ditched his shift!

21
00:00:51,765 --> 00:00:53,815
If you mean Lucha,
isn't that him over there?

22
00:01:00,345 --> 00:01:01,755
What's wrong with him?

23
00:01:02,985 --> 00:01:07,355
The girl he likes just
came by to buy yakisoba.

24
00:01:07,785 --> 00:01:09,095
With her boyfriend, no less.

25
00:01:14,555 --> 00:01:18,365
Wonder if he can pull himself
together before the headline act...

26
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:22,205
By the way, where's Saeko?

27
00:01:23,045 --> 00:01:24,945
Looks like she's not here yet.

28
00:01:25,675 --> 00:01:28,545
Worst case, Saeko might
have to fill in on vocals.

29
00:02:05,795 --> 00:02:13,295
"How Do We Relationship?"

30
00:02:18,788 --> 00:02:23,768
[Episode 6: Loving You, Having Loved You]

31
00:02:23,965 --> 00:02:25,925
Muscles! You definitely
don't have enough muscle!

32
00:02:26,035 --> 00:02:28,205
Isn't it because you don't
have enough muscle?

33
00:02:40,315 --> 00:02:41,785
- Look...
- Um...

34
00:02:52,185 --> 00:02:53,385
About yesterday...

35
00:02:53,835 --> 00:02:54,935
I'm sorry.

36
00:02:56,865 --> 00:02:58,365
There's something...

37
00:02:58,935 --> 00:03:00,905
I have to tell you myself.

38
00:03:03,145 --> 00:03:04,645
I'm sorry too.

39
00:03:05,505 --> 00:03:06,615
Let's just

40
00:03:07,205 --> 00:03:08,475
lay everything out honestly.

41
00:03:09,175 --> 00:03:11,385
I've braced myself.

42
00:03:13,255 --> 00:03:16,015
Being honest with each
other is what couples do, right?

43
00:03:19,225 --> 00:03:20,725
At the reunion...

44
00:03:21,555 --> 00:03:23,295
Nothing really happened.

45
00:03:25,165 --> 00:03:26,165
It's just...

46
00:03:27,365 --> 00:03:29,465
talking with senpai,

47
00:03:30,965 --> 00:03:32,365
I couldn't help remembering.

48
00:03:34,775 --> 00:03:35,935
Remembering what?

49
00:03:38,645 --> 00:03:39,845
That feeling back then...

50
00:03:39,915 --> 00:03:41,015
when my heart fluttered.

51
00:03:43,285 --> 00:03:44,285
I'm sorry.

52
00:03:46,085 --> 00:03:47,385
Back then...

53
00:03:48,955 --> 00:03:50,455
for a split second,

54
00:03:52,355 --> 00:03:54,755
I felt like... I might still like her...

55
00:03:58,525 --> 00:04:00,065
Yeah... And then?

56
00:04:00,545 --> 00:04:01,545
And then...

57
00:04:02,805 --> 00:04:03,805
But I...

58
00:04:04,965 --> 00:04:07,375
realized right away
that it was totally wrong.

59
00:04:08,575 --> 00:04:11,145
I haven't contacted her since.

60
00:04:14,645 --> 00:04:18,114
Who tells their own girlfriend
that they like another girl?

61
00:04:18,115 --> 00:04:19,385
You're honest to a fault.

62
00:04:22,725 --> 00:04:23,755
Well...

63
00:04:24,355 --> 00:04:25,355
Then again...

64
00:04:26,235 --> 00:04:29,795
I'm probably the idiot
for pressing you when I already knew.

65
00:04:36,165 --> 00:04:37,805
You're mad, aren't you?

66
00:04:41,625 --> 00:04:43,205
I want to throw a fit, sure,

67
00:04:43,445 --> 00:04:45,775
but throwing a fit won't change anything.

68
00:04:49,945 --> 00:04:50,945
I'm sorry...

69
00:04:56,725 --> 00:04:57,725
Miwa.

70
00:04:58,415 --> 00:05:01,995
You chose me over her, right?

71
00:05:03,855 --> 00:05:04,665
Yeah.

72
00:05:04,865 --> 00:05:05,965
Yes, I did.

73
00:05:06,335 --> 00:05:07,565
Then we're fine.

74
00:05:08,535 --> 00:05:11,605
We've made up!

75
00:05:17,205 --> 00:05:18,975
What a relief...

76
00:05:20,275 --> 00:05:23,315
I was sure you were
going to break up with me.

77
00:05:24,385 --> 00:05:27,214
I don't want to break up with you...

78
00:05:27,215 --> 00:05:30,185
Hey, don't cry.

79
00:05:32,895 --> 00:05:35,495
Now that I'm relieved, I
just couldn't stop the tears...

80
00:05:40,165 --> 00:05:41,165
You know,

81
00:05:41,695 --> 00:05:44,265
I've never heard you say you like me.

82
00:05:46,235 --> 00:05:47,235
No way...

83
00:05:47,535 --> 00:05:48,635
I'm sure I have.

84
00:05:48,675 --> 00:05:51,575
Nope! Not once!

85
00:05:53,045 --> 00:05:54,345
Then I'll say it now...

86
00:05:55,075 --> 00:05:56,145
Don't bother.

87
00:05:56,285 --> 00:05:58,445
It doesn't count if you have to be coerced.

88
00:05:58,545 --> 00:05:59,685
Let's go.

89
00:06:04,685 --> 00:06:05,685
I like you.

90
00:06:06,135 --> 00:06:07,135
Saeko.

91
00:06:07,995 --> 00:06:08,995
I love you.

92
00:06:10,995 --> 00:06:13,065
That was... so half-assed!

93
00:06:13,095 --> 00:06:15,895
What was that? Zero emotion!

94
00:06:16,715 --> 00:06:18,014
You too, Saeko.

95
00:06:18,015 --> 00:06:19,934
You've never told me you like me either!

96
00:06:19,935 --> 00:06:22,214
Huh? Really?

97
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,705
Say it then!

98
00:06:25,895 --> 00:06:27,175
I like you.

99
00:06:27,245 --> 00:06:31,285
I like you so, so much!

100
00:06:31,385 --> 00:06:34,285
Come on, Saeko, you're
being just as half-hearted!

101
00:06:45,065 --> 00:06:46,625
It's all Lucha's fault anyway!

102
00:06:46,665 --> 00:06:48,694
Here we go, here we go!

103
00:06:48,695 --> 00:06:50,005
Ready, set, go!

104
00:06:50,065 --> 00:06:52,505
Hey, Miwa, don't just stand there filming!

105
00:06:52,805 --> 00:06:55,375
We are Lightning Rabbit!

106
00:06:55,475 --> 00:06:56,505
Rabbit!

107
00:06:56,845 --> 00:06:58,404
That's our Rika!

108
00:06:58,405 --> 00:06:59,775
So avant-garde!

109
00:07:03,295 --> 00:07:04,295
What is this?

110
00:07:04,445 --> 00:07:05,765
Hey, what is this supposed to be?

111
00:07:06,585 --> 00:07:07,855
It's a dragon!

112
00:07:09,825 --> 00:07:11,784
Pass it here. Miwa, you
write something too!

113
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:12,785
Here, here.

114
00:07:13,855 --> 00:07:15,655
Your turn, Miwa!

115
00:07:15,895 --> 00:07:17,695
What should I draw?

116
00:07:17,725 --> 00:07:18,725
Draw a dog.

117
00:07:18,895 --> 00:07:20,495
Oh, that's so cute!

118
00:07:20,595 --> 00:07:21,595
Super cute.

119
00:07:22,635 --> 00:07:24,065
I'm so beat!

120
00:07:25,505 --> 00:07:29,675
We don't have booth duty
tomorrow, let's explore properly!

121
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:31,845
Sounds good.

122
00:07:32,075 --> 00:07:33,944
I want to go to the haunted house!

123
00:07:33,945 --> 00:07:36,285
Um, the haunted house is a bit...

124
00:07:39,585 --> 00:07:40,815
Saeko.

125
00:07:42,075 --> 00:07:43,075
Um...

126
00:07:43,325 --> 00:07:45,555
You don't have work today, right?

127
00:07:45,955 --> 00:07:47,475
Want to stay over at my place tonight?

128
00:07:49,055 --> 00:07:50,565
Sure, but why all of a sudden?

129
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,465
Well, no reason.

130
00:07:52,795 --> 00:07:53,795
Is that a no?

131
00:07:56,865 --> 00:07:57,865
Miwa.

132
00:07:58,235 --> 00:07:59,705
Do you like me?

133
00:08:01,775 --> 00:08:02,945
Again?

134
00:08:05,345 --> 00:08:06,445
Of course I do.

135
00:08:06,675 --> 00:08:07,675
I like you the most.

136
00:08:27,565 --> 00:08:28,835
What's wrong?

137
00:08:30,805 --> 00:08:32,365
Times like this,

138
00:08:32,505 --> 00:08:35,274
it really hits me that I'm dating a girl.

139
00:08:35,275 --> 00:08:36,845
And it feels really nice.

140
00:08:46,145 --> 00:08:48,585
It just hit me...

141
00:08:50,025 --> 00:08:54,225
I'm really so happy right now.

142
00:08:58,415 --> 00:09:00,865
Are you... really happy?

143
00:09:10,305 --> 00:09:11,305
Yeah.

144
00:09:12,695 --> 00:09:13,695
Because...

145
00:09:13,795 --> 00:09:15,145
not that long ago,

146
00:09:15,375 --> 00:09:19,185
I never even imagined I could
actually get a girlfriend like this.

147
00:09:21,385 --> 00:09:23,785
So you're happy just because
you get to date a girl?

148
00:09:26,455 --> 00:09:27,695
No, that's not it.

149
00:09:28,855 --> 00:09:31,795
It's because it's you, Saeko.
That's why it's great.

150
00:09:32,455 --> 00:09:33,455
Because you're...

151
00:09:34,135 --> 00:09:36,965
so gentle, and such
a wonderful person...

152
00:09:36,966 --> 00:09:38,935
You don't have to force yourself anymore.

153
00:09:41,875 --> 00:09:44,575
You're just trying to
convince yourself, aren't you?

154
00:09:45,375 --> 00:09:48,455
You can't keep going unless you brainwash
yourself into feeling happy, right?

155
00:09:50,695 --> 00:09:51,645
If this keeps up...

156
00:09:51,685 --> 00:09:52,915
I really can't take it.

157
00:09:53,755 --> 00:09:55,185
Actually... I've truly had enough.

158
00:09:57,855 --> 00:09:59,055
Saeko...?

159
00:10:03,225 --> 00:10:04,425
Let's break up.

160
00:10:05,225 --> 00:10:06,795
Please break up with me.

161
00:10:08,335 --> 00:10:09,335
No!

162
00:10:09,615 --> 00:10:10,924
I don't want to break up!

163
00:10:10,925 --> 00:10:12,165
Stay with me!

164
00:10:14,235 --> 00:10:15,405
Why are you doing this?

165
00:10:16,745 --> 00:10:18,204
Saeko, please!

166
00:10:18,205 --> 00:10:19,205
I like you!

167
00:10:20,715 --> 00:10:22,645
Hey, I really do like you!

168
00:10:23,845 --> 00:10:24,845
But...

169
00:10:25,415 --> 00:10:27,055
that's not romantic love at all.

170
00:10:30,325 --> 00:10:31,655
How can you say that...?

171
00:10:33,655 --> 00:10:35,195
You're too easy to read, Miwa.

172
00:10:36,095 --> 00:10:37,895
I can see right through you.

173
00:10:42,115 --> 00:10:43,965
Let's talk properly another day.

174
00:10:44,105 --> 00:10:45,995
Wait, don't go!

175
00:10:46,505 --> 00:10:47,604
Please...

176
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:48,875
Just leave me alone.

177
00:10:58,695 --> 00:11:00,285
Fresh yakisoba, hot off the grill!

178
00:11:00,915 --> 00:11:02,715
Yakisoba available! Come get yours!

179
00:11:02,815 --> 00:11:05,055
Why is Saeko the one cooking?

180
00:11:05,525 --> 00:11:07,195
Weren't you on shift yesterday?

181
00:11:08,595 --> 00:11:09,954
Well...

182
00:11:09,955 --> 00:11:11,595
I was late yesterday.

183
00:11:11,765 --> 00:11:14,635
Skipped the first half,
so I'm making up for it!

184
00:11:14,995 --> 00:11:16,265
I see...

185
00:11:16,905 --> 00:11:19,035
Is your band gonna be okay, though?

186
00:11:19,335 --> 00:11:20,335
Huh?

187
00:11:20,655 --> 00:11:23,305
Lucha's nursing a broken heart,

188
00:11:23,345 --> 00:11:26,745
and didn't Miwa call in sick today?

189
00:11:29,305 --> 00:11:30,305
Well...

190
00:11:30,415 --> 00:11:31,915
We'll manage somehow!

191
00:11:32,855 --> 00:11:36,215
By the way, if you're so free,
help me bring in some customers!

192
00:11:36,425 --> 00:11:37,584
No way!

193
00:11:37,585 --> 00:11:39,795
Rika is off the clock right now!

194
00:11:40,695 --> 00:11:42,695
Hey, Rika!

195
00:11:42,895 --> 00:11:44,865
I'm swamped here!

196
00:12:33,615 --> 00:12:35,845
I'm all on my own...

197
00:12:40,655 --> 00:12:42,925
Saeko, you've gone down
the slide way too many times.

198
00:12:42,955 --> 00:12:45,525
Yuria, don't you want to date someone?

199
00:12:45,855 --> 00:12:47,895
I do! Totally want to!

200
00:12:47,955 --> 00:12:49,054
Do you like anyone?

201
00:12:49,055 --> 00:12:50,124
Ever confessed to someone?

202
00:12:50,125 --> 00:12:51,464
Nope.

203
00:12:51,465 --> 00:12:53,565
Never confessed, never been confessed to.

204
00:12:54,035 --> 00:12:55,334
Makes sense.

205
00:12:55,335 --> 00:12:58,565
Being single is pretty common these days.

206
00:12:59,065 --> 00:13:01,025
Yeah...

207
00:13:03,205 --> 00:13:05,705
I used to think so too.

208
00:13:06,875 --> 00:13:10,345
But I still can't help feeling anxious.

209
00:13:11,245 --> 00:13:12,245
Anxious?

210
00:13:12,315 --> 00:13:13,315
Yeah.

211
00:13:14,445 --> 00:13:15,855
I keep feeling like

212
00:13:16,085 --> 00:13:19,895
maybe I'm the only person in the world
who isn't loved by anyone.

213
00:13:27,965 --> 00:13:29,605
Whoa, wait! You startled me!

214
00:13:30,785 --> 00:13:31,785
Look at you!

215
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:34,465
Sorry for getting so
depressing all of a sudden.

216
00:13:36,995 --> 00:13:41,575
Even though I've dated,
it's not like she truly loved me either.

217
00:13:41,915 --> 00:13:44,015
What? That's awful!

218
00:13:44,645 --> 00:13:47,385
Want me to beat up
that ex-boyfriend for you?

219
00:13:47,525 --> 00:13:50,285
Wait, beating someone up is barbaric!

220
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:51,955
Huh?

221
00:13:54,255 --> 00:13:55,955
Wait, is this why
nobody wants me?

222
00:13:56,425 --> 00:13:57,925
Uh, how would I know?

223
00:14:00,695 --> 00:14:02,064
What a blow!

224
00:14:02,065 --> 00:14:03,935
Don't take it so hard!

225
00:14:18,465 --> 00:14:19,565
Actually...

226
00:14:20,765 --> 00:14:24,485
I don't blame her at all.

227
00:14:26,525 --> 00:14:30,595
She really is kind of a handful, though.

228
00:14:31,785 --> 00:14:34,035
Yet... she's so shy,

229
00:14:34,435 --> 00:14:35,895
and strangely earnest.

230
00:14:36,765 --> 00:14:38,305
Her head's full of romantic fantasies,

231
00:14:39,685 --> 00:14:43,005
and despite looking mature,
she's like a kid on the inside.

232
00:14:44,305 --> 00:14:46,875
Everything's written on her
face. She can't hide a thing.

233
00:14:49,345 --> 00:14:50,345
And yet...

234
00:14:51,445 --> 00:14:52,845
for some reason...

235
00:14:54,085 --> 00:14:56,455
all of that put together

236
00:14:58,055 --> 00:15:00,295
just made me adore her so much...

237
00:15:02,555 --> 00:15:03,725
Saeko...

238
00:15:09,195 --> 00:15:10,765
Though it's too late for all that now!

239
00:15:13,385 --> 00:15:16,845
Damn it!

240
00:15:29,725 --> 00:15:31,285
Screw this!

241
00:15:34,825 --> 00:15:36,725
I just wanted to be loved too...

242
00:16:18,605 --> 00:16:20,035
Hey, Saeko.

243
00:16:21,445 --> 00:16:22,545
Why?

244
00:16:24,675 --> 00:16:25,945
We were...

245
00:16:27,475 --> 00:16:29,575
getting along so well, weren't we?

246
00:16:32,525 --> 00:16:35,785
Were you, though? It
felt pretty forced, didn't it?

247
00:16:37,125 --> 00:16:40,055
Honestly, it didn't look like
you liked your girlfriend at all.

248
00:16:41,555 --> 00:16:43,125
That's not true...

249
00:16:43,325 --> 00:16:46,635
The one you really like is
that senpai from before, isn't it?

250
00:16:47,395 --> 00:16:49,171
Have you ever felt your heart
flutter for your current girlfriend

251
00:16:49,195 --> 00:16:52,135
the way it did for senpai?

252
00:16:53,435 --> 00:16:54,435
But...

253
00:16:54,975 --> 00:16:56,975
I have fun being with her.

254
00:16:57,045 --> 00:16:58,045
Yeah.

255
00:16:58,945 --> 00:17:01,175
And she's so kind.

256
00:17:02,245 --> 00:17:04,615
There's so much to look up to...

257
00:17:05,745 --> 00:17:07,085
I see.

258
00:17:07,185 --> 00:17:08,715
You're really fond of her.

259
00:17:10,755 --> 00:17:11,755
Yeah.

260
00:17:13,995 --> 00:17:14,995
And then what?

261
00:17:16,595 --> 00:17:18,825
Are you truly happy from
the bottom of your heart?

262
00:17:31,805 --> 00:17:34,575
Sorry for bursting into tears like this.

263
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:36,845
Annoying, right?

264
00:17:37,045 --> 00:17:39,555
Like I'm the tragic heroine of some drama.

265
00:17:39,565 --> 00:17:41,315
Not annoying at all!

266
00:17:42,015 --> 00:17:44,015
What's wrong with being
the tragic heroine anyway?

267
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:48,795
Besides, people are supposed
to cry when they're sad.

268
00:17:55,185 --> 00:17:56,605
That's true...

269
00:17:57,305 --> 00:17:58,935
It's okay to cry, right?

270
00:18:01,845 --> 00:18:03,004
Hey, Saeko!

271
00:18:03,005 --> 00:18:04,321
Want to go blow off some steam at karaoke?

272
00:18:04,345 --> 00:18:06,874
But with the festival tomorrow,
I might have to sing on stage.

273
00:18:06,875 --> 00:18:09,815
Man, I really want some yakisoba too!

274
00:18:10,115 --> 00:18:11,121
I'll make you some next time.

275
00:18:11,145 --> 00:18:12,385
Wait, really?

276
00:18:21,295 --> 00:18:23,365
Saeko smiling so
brightly like that...

277
00:18:26,345 --> 00:18:31,665
when was the last time
I saw [her like that]?

278
00:18:49,825 --> 00:18:52,995
Anyway... let's just break up.

279
00:18:53,395 --> 00:18:54,395
That's all.

280
00:18:59,025 --> 00:19:02,135
Don't look like it's the end of the world.

281
00:19:03,945 --> 00:19:04,945
Because...

282
00:19:06,065 --> 00:19:09,875
it's my first breakup ever.

283
00:19:10,405 --> 00:19:12,304
We're just going back to being friends.

284
00:19:12,305 --> 00:19:14,015
Just be natural, like we always are.

285
00:19:16,445 --> 00:19:17,515
That's true.

286
00:19:17,915 --> 00:19:18,915
I'm sorry...

287
00:19:19,015 --> 00:19:20,914
I told you to stop apologizing!

288
00:19:20,915 --> 00:19:22,485
No more "I'm sorry"!

289
00:19:39,335 --> 00:19:42,405
Want to watch some funny clips?

290
00:19:44,045 --> 00:19:45,505
Funny clips...?

291
00:19:48,575 --> 00:19:49,575
Ah.

292
00:19:49,685 --> 00:19:50,785
This one, look!

293
00:19:58,185 --> 00:19:59,484
Wait, play it again!

294
00:19:59,485 --> 00:20:00,595
Again?

295
00:20:03,905 --> 00:20:05,525
It's so dumb, but hilarious, right?

296
00:20:16,745 --> 00:20:17,745
What's wrong?

297
00:20:20,175 --> 00:20:21,175
Nothing.

298
00:20:22,265 --> 00:20:23,265
I just felt like...

299
00:20:24,985 --> 00:20:27,555
it's been a while since I saw you smile.

300
00:20:28,015 --> 00:20:31,755
Wait, am I usually that stone-faced?

301
00:20:32,925 --> 00:20:34,255
Even if you say that...

302
00:20:38,265 --> 00:20:41,295
you really never looked at me,
did you, Miwa?

303
00:20:46,375 --> 00:20:47,675
You're right...

304
00:20:57,985 --> 00:20:59,185
That look in your eyes...

305
00:20:59,915 --> 00:21:02,855
I absolutely despise it...

306
00:21:05,845 --> 00:21:06,845
Ouch!

307
00:21:08,885 --> 00:21:10,795
Come on, our set's starting soon!

308
00:21:10,825 --> 00:21:12,365
Pull yourself together!

309
00:21:25,885 --> 00:21:27,415
Still not working, huh...

310
00:21:30,285 --> 00:21:32,485
Pull this again and you're fired!

311
00:21:33,615 --> 00:21:34,755
I'm sorry...

312
00:21:37,185 --> 00:21:38,255
Whatever.

313
00:21:38,785 --> 00:21:41,495
I felt like screaming my lungs out anyway!

314
00:21:43,505 --> 00:21:44,595
All right!

315
00:21:44,665 --> 00:21:45,725
Let's do this, everyone!

316
00:21:48,095 --> 00:21:49,095
Come on.

317
00:21:49,135 --> 00:21:50,135
You too, Lucha!

318
00:21:51,805 --> 00:21:53,575
How long are you gonna keep crying?

319
00:21:54,435 --> 00:21:55,435
Hands in!

320
00:21:55,675 --> 00:21:56,675
Let's go!

321
00:21:58,165 --> 00:21:59,165
Yeah!

322
00:22:00,715 --> 00:22:01,715
Yeah!

323
00:22:03,245 --> 00:22:08,385
Lightning Rabbit, go!

324
00:22:22,095 --> 00:22:27,305
♪ Hey, if the world were to end today, ♪

325
00:22:27,475 --> 00:22:32,675
♪ who would you choose
to have by your side? ♪

326
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:35,044
♪ Hey, whether it's music ♪

327
00:22:35,045 --> 00:22:38,444
♪ or your favorite chocolate cake, ♪

328
00:22:38,445 --> 00:22:40,584
♪ I'll be waiting for you right here. ♪

329
00:22:40,585 --> 00:22:42,185
♪ So look at me. ♪

330
00:22:44,105 --> 00:22:49,225
♪ If you had shown me
your tears back then, ♪

331
00:22:49,255 --> 00:22:53,195
♪ whether time or love, ♪

332
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:55,094
♪ I would've poured it all into you. ♪

333
00:22:55,095 --> 00:23:00,575
♪ Until this day comes to an end, ♪

334
00:23:00,585 --> 00:23:03,604
♪ please take my hand ♪

335
00:23:03,605 --> 00:23:06,315
♪ as if nothing had ever happened. ♪

336
00:23:06,345 --> 00:23:11,584
♪ Even when tomorrow arrives, ♪

337
00:23:11,585 --> 00:23:14,484
♪ please tell me
everything is just the same. ♪

338
00:23:14,485 --> 00:23:18,625
♪ Because this dream will never end, ♪

339
00:23:19,505 --> 00:23:24,095
♪ no matter how long,
we'll always be together. ♪

340
00:23:45,685 --> 00:23:47,555
[Next Episode Preview] It's already
been a month since we broke up.

341
00:23:47,565 --> 00:23:49,655
We were supposed to be strangers again.

342
00:23:49,755 --> 00:23:50,964
We're bandmates!

343
00:23:50,988 --> 00:23:51,988
Bandmates...?

344
00:23:52,755 --> 00:23:53,825
Let's go!

345
00:23:53,855 --> 00:23:55,744
So greedy and selfish.

346
00:23:55,745 --> 00:23:57,945
There's something really off
about you right now, Miwa.

347
00:23:58,245 --> 00:23:59,765
Shiho senpai.
